# One rule for line endings, enforced by git rather than by whoever edits
# next.
#
# Every text file is stored with LF and checked out with LF, on every
# platform. Without this the repo had a mix — some files CRLF, some LF,
# one with both — and any tool that rewrote a file whole normalized it to
# whatever it felt like, so a two-line change arrived as a nine-hundred
# line diff and the real edit was impossible to see in review.
#
# LF rather than CRLF because that is what CI builds and lints with, and
# what every Rust toolchain emits; git for Windows and every editor in
# use here read LF without complaint.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Images are binary: never touch their bytes.
*.png binary
